I'm noticing there's a discrepancy between the comments in the test file and the card implementation—both say "another source" when the actual oracle text specifies "another creature." The code itself handles this correctly by only applying the damage multiplier when creatures deal damage to other creatures, so non-creature sources don't trigger this effect anyway. Both are correct. The second ability only triggers when a creature deals damage to the equipped creature, so there's no need for a check in the player damage function. Now I'm wondering if there are other code paths where damage gets dealt to a creature outside of `deal_damage_to_creature`—the `fight` function also calls it, so combat damage there would be doubled too, but let me trace through this more carefully.

